// gpupart: the sample of a program package with a gpu/ folder, a part in
// two halves. src/ runs on the CPU; gpu/ (gpu/pattern.cone) is the GPU half,
// which Congo checks against the GPU's rules, compiles into this program as
// the submodule 'pattern', and compiles for the GPU, without src/ and so
// without 'main', into build/<mode>/gpupart.spv beside the program.
//
// main (src/main.cone) runs pattern's kernel 'fill' on the GPU through
// gpuwork, calls pattern's 'cell', the function the kernel is made from, on
// the CPU, and compares every word: they must be identical. Congo's own
// tests run it (tools/congo/test_congo.py), since a test program cannot
// import an executable package. It needs a GPU driver with Vulkan 1.3 and
// SDL3.dll; with the Vulkan SDK, the validation layers are on, and must say
// nothing. GPUWORK_REPORT set prints the adapter too.

mod gpupart;

import testing use *;
import stdio use *;
import libc;
import collections use List;
import gpu use *;
import gpuwork use *;

// The GPU half's types, the one declaration both halves share
use pattern Settings, Cell;
